{
  "title": "35: Faatir فاطر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاَ لْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ فَاطِرِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ جَاعِلِ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ رُسُلًا اُولِىْۤ اَجْنِحَةٍ مَّثْنٰى وَثُلٰثَ وَرُبٰعَ ؕ يَزِيْدُ فِى الْخَلْقِ مَا يَشَآءُ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(1)\nA’ZAABAN LHAMDU LILLAAHE FAATERE SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE JAAE’ELE MALAA-EKATE ROSOLAN OOLEE AAJNEHATIN MMASNAA WASULAASA WARUBAAA’A YAZEEDU FIL AL-KHALQE MAA YASHAAA INNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\n(All) praise is God’s, the Originator of the heavens and the earth, the Maker of the angels, messengers flying on wings, two, and three, and four: He addeth to His creation whatever He willeth; Verily God, over all things hath power.\nمَا يَفْتَحِ اللّٰهُ لِلنَّاسِ مِنْ رَّحْمَةٍ فَلَا مُمْسِكَ لَهَاۚ وَمَا يُمْسِكْ ۙ فَلَا مُرْسِلَ لَهٗ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهؕ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(2)\nMAA YAFTAHE LAAHO LIN-NAASE MIN RRAHMATIN FALAA MUMSEKA LAHAA WA MAA YUMSEK FALAA MURSELA LAHU MIN BAA’DEH WA HOWA A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nWhatever God layeth open of His mercy unto the people, there is none to hold it back, and whatever He holdeth back there is none to send it forth after that, and He is the All- Mighty, the All-Wise.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اذْكُرُوْا نِعْمَتَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْؕ هَلْ مِنْ خَالِقٍ غَيْرُ اللّٰهِ يَرْزُقُكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَۖ فَاَنّٰى تُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏(3)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO KOROO NEA’MATAL LAAHE A’LAYKUM HAL MIN KHAALEQIN GHAYRO LAAHE YARZOQOKUM MENAL SAMAAA-E WAL ARZ LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA FA-ANNAA TUFAKOONA.\nO’ ye people! Remember ye God’s bounty on you; Is there any creator other than God who provideth you with your sustenance from the heaven and the earth? There is no god but He; Whence then are ye turned away (from the truth)?\nوَاِنْ يُّكَذِّبُوْكَ فَقَدْ كُذِّبَتْ رُسُلٌ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَؕ وَاِلَى اللّٰهِ تُرْجَعُ الْاُمُوْرُ‏(4)\nWA YYUKAZZEBOOKA FAQAD KUZZEBAT RUSULUN MIN QABLEKA WA ELAL LAAHE TURJA-U’L OMOOR.\nAnd if they belie thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) indeed have been belied apostles before thee; and unto God (alone) are returned all affairs!\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ فَلَا تَغُرَّنَّكُمُ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَاوَلَا يَغُرَّنَّكُمْ بِاللّٰهِ الْغَرُوْرُ‏(5)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO INNAL WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN FALAA TAGHURRANNAKUMU HAYAATUD AD-DUNYAAWALAA YAGHURRANNAKUM BIL-LAAHE AL-GHAROORU.\nO’ ye people! verily the promise of God is true, so let not the life of this world beguile you; and let not the Arch-Beguiler (Satan) beguile you about God!\nاِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ فَاتَّخِذُوْهُ عَدُوًّا ؕ اِنَّمَا يَدْعُوْا حِزْبَهٗ لِيَكُوْنُوْا مِنْ اَصْحٰبِ السَّعِيْرِؕ‏(6)\nINNAL ASH-SHAYTAANA LAKUM A’DUWWUM FAATTAKHEZOOHU A’DUWWAL INNAMAA YAD-O’O HEZBAH LEEKOONOOA MIN ASHAABIL AS-SAE’EERE.\nVerily Satan is your enemy, so ye (too) take him (as your) enemy; He only inviteth his party that they may be the fellows of the flaming fire.\nاَ لَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ شَدِيْدٌ ؕ وَّالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوْا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّاَجْرٌ كَبِيْرٌ‏(7)\nA’ZAABAN LLAZEENA KAFAROO LAHUM A’ZAABUN SHADEEDUN WWAALLAZEENA AAMANUT AAMANOO SAALEHAATE LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WA AJRUN KABEER.\nThose who disbelieve, for them shall be a severe chastisement; And as for those who believe and do good, for them shall be forgiveness and a great recompense.\nاَفَمَنْ زُيِّنَ لَهٗ سُوْٓءُ عَمَلِهٖ فَرَاٰهُ حَسَنًا ؕ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُضِلُّ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ‌ۖ  فَلَا تَذْهَبْ نَفْسُكَ عَلَيْهِمْ حَسَرٰتٍ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِمَا يَصْنَعُوْنَ‏(8)\nAFAMAWN ZUYYENA LAHU SOOO-UL A’AMALEH FA RA-AAHO HASANAN FA-INNAL LAAHA YOZILLO MAN YASHAAA-O WA YAHDEE MAN YASHAAA-O FALAA TAZHAB NAFSUKA A’LAYHIM A’LAYHIM INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM BEMAA YASNAU’OONA.\nWhat! Is he then whose evil deed is made alluring that he beholdeth it good (equal to the one guided aright)! (Nay! by no means!), for verily God leaveth to stray whomsoever He willeth and guideth He whomsoever He willeth, so let not thy self go (in vain) in grief for them; Verily God knoweth all that they do.\nوَاللّٰهُ الَّذِىْۤ اَرْسَلَ الرِّيٰحَ فَتُثِيْرُ سَحَابًا فَسُقْنٰهُ اِلٰى بَلَدٍ مَّيِّتٍ فَاَحْيَيْنَا بِهِ الْاَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ النُّشُوْرُ‏(9)\nWAL LAAHO LAZEE ARSALA REYAAHA FA-TOSEERO SAHAABAN FASUQNAAHU ELAA BALADIN MMAYTIN FAAHYAYNAA BEHIL ARZA BA’DA MAWTEHAA KAZAALEKA NOSHOOR.\nAnd God is He Who sendeth the winds and they raise the clouds, then We drive them on to a country (which is) dead, and give We life therewith to the earth after its death; Even so is the (rising of the dead in) Resurrection.\nمَنْ كَانَ يُرِيْدُ الْعِزَّةَ فَلِلّٰهِ الْعِزَّةُ جَمِيْعًا ؕ اِلَيْهِ يَصْعَدُ الْكَلِمُ الطَّيِّبُ وَالْعَمَلُ الصَّالِحُ يَرْفَعُهٗ ؕ وَ الَّذِيْنَ يَمْكُرُوْنَ السَّيِّاٰتِ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ شَدِيْدٌ  ؕ وَمَكْرُ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُوَ يَبُوْرُ‏(10)\nMAN KAANA YOREEDO AL-E’EZZATA FALILLAAHE I’ZZATO JAMEE-A’A ELAYHE YASA’ADU AL-KALEMU AT-TAYBU WAL A’AMALU AS-SAALEHU YARFAU’UH WA LAZEENA YAMKOROON SAYYE-AATE LAHUM A’ZAABUN SHADEEDUN WAMAKRU OOLAAA-EKA HOWA YABOORU.\nWhosoever desireth honour (let him seek it from God, for) God’s (alone) is all honour; Unto Him (only) ascend all good words; and as for those who plot evil deeds, for them shall be a severe chastisement; and their plot, it shall be vain.\nوَاللّٰهُ خَلَقَكُمْ مِّنْ تُرَابٍ ثُمَّ مِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ ثُمَّ جَعَلَكُمْ اَزْوَاجًا ؕ وَمَا تَحْمِلُ مِنْ اُنْثٰى وَلَا تَضَعُ اِلَّا بِعِلْمِهؕ وَمَا يُعَمَّرُ مِنْ مُّعَمَّرٍ وَّلَا يُنْقَصُ مِنْ عُمُرِهٖۤ اِلَّا فِىْ كِتٰبٍؕ اِنَّ ذٰلِكَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ يَسِيْرٌ‏(11)\nWAL LAAHO KHALAQAKUM MIN TORAABIN SUMMA MIN NUTFATIN SUMMA JAA’ALAKUM AZWAAJANW WA MAA TAHMELO MIN UNSAA WA LAA TAZAA-O’ ILLAA BEE’ELMEH WA MAA YO-A’MMARO MIN MMUA’AMMARIN WA LAA YUNQASU MIN U’UMUREH ILLAA FEE KETAABIN INNAL ZAALEKA A’LAL LAAHE YASEERUN.\nAnd God created you of dust, then of the life-germ, then He made you pairs (of male and female); and a female beareth not, nor doth she deliver, save with His knowledge; and ageth not the aged, nor finisheth from any one’s life, but it is all in a Book (decree ordained); Verily this, for God, is easy.\nوَمَا يَسْتَوِىْ الْبَحْرٰنِ ‌ۖ  هٰذَا عَذْبٌ فُرَاتٌ سَآئِغٌ شَرَابُهٗ وَ هٰذَا مِلْحٌ اُجَاجٌ ؕ وَمِنْ كُلٍّ تَاْكُلُوْنَ لَحْمًا طَرِيًّا وَّتَسْتَخْرِجُوْنَ حِلْيَةً تَلْبَسُوْنَهَا ۚ وَتَرَى الْفُلْكَ فِيْهِ مَوَاخِرَ لِتَبْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA MAA YASTAWEE AL-BAHRAANE HAAZAA A’AZBUN FURAATUN SAAEGHUN SHARAABUH WA HAAZAA MELHUN AUJAAJUN WA MIN KULLIN TAAKULOONA SUMMA NAKSOOHAA TAREEA WWATASTAKHREJOONA HELYATAN TALBASOONAHAA WA TARAL AL-FULKA FEEHE MAWAAKHERA LE-TABTAGHOO MIN FAZLEHI WA LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nAnd nor are the two seas alike, this one (is) sweet, quencheth thirst its sweetness, (and) pleasant to drink, and the other salt, and bitter; and yet from them both, eat ye flesh fresh and take forth ornaments which wear ye; and seest thou the ships cleave through it, that ye may seek of His grace, and that ye may be grateful.\nيُوْلِجُ الَّيْلَ فِى النَّهَارِ وَيُوْلِجُ النَّهَارَ فِى الَّيْلِ ۙ وَسَخَّرَ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ ‌ۖ  كُلٌّ يَّجْرِىْ لِاَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى ؕ ذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمْ لَهُ الْمُلْكُ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ مَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ مِنْ قِطْمِيْرٍؕ‏(13)\nYOOLEJU LAYLA FIL AN-NAHAARE WAYOOLEJU NAHAARA FIL LAYLE SAKHKHARASH SHAMSA WAL QAMARA KULLUL YYAJREAA LE-ELAA AJALIM ZAA LEKUMU LAAHO RABBOKUM LAHUL A’LAYNAA WAL LAZEENA TADU’OONA MIN DOONEHI MAA YAMLEKOONA MIN QETMEERIN.\nCauseth He the night to enter into the day, and the day to enter into the night, and hath made He subservient (unto you) the sun and the moon; each travelleth to an appointed time: This is God your Lord! His is the kingdom; and those whom ye call upon other than Him, own not (even) a straw.\nاِنْ تَدْعُوْهُمْ لَا يَسْمَعُوْا دُعَآءَكُمْ‌ ۚ وَلَوْ سَمِعُوْا مَا اسْتَجَابُوْا لَكُمْ ؕ وَيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ يَكْفُرُوْنَ بِشِرْكِكُمْ ؕ وَلَا يُنَبِّئُكَ مِثْلُ خَبِيْرٍ‏(14)\nIN TADU’OOHUM LAA YASMAU’OOA DUA’AAAKUM WA LAW SAMEO’O MAA ASTAJAABOOA LAKUM WA YAWMA QEYAAMATE YAKFOROON BESHERKEKUM WA LAA YUNABBEUKA LAZEE KHABEERIN.\nIf ye call on them they shall hear not your call; and even if they hear they shall answer you not; and on the Day of Judgment they will deny your associating them (with God), and none can (ever) inform thee as (the One Who is) the All-Aware.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اَنْتُمُ الْفُقَرَآءُ اِلَى اللّٰهِۚ وَاللّٰهُ هُوَ الْغَنِىُّ الْحَمِيْدُ‏(15)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO AANTUMU AL-FUQARAAU ELAL LAAHE WAL LAAHO HOWA AL-GHANEAAAU AL-HAMEEDU.\nO’ ye people! ye are the needy unto God; and God (alone) is He Who is the Self-Sufficient, the Most Praised One.\nاِنْ يَّشَاْ يُذْهِبْكُمْ وَيَاْتِ بِخَلْقٍ جَدِيْدٍۚ‏(16)\nINY YASHAA-A YUZHIBKUM WA YAA-TE BEKHALQIN JADEED.\nIf He willeth, He will take you off and bring a new creation.\nوَمَا ذٰ لِكَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ بِعَزِيْزٍ‏(17)\nWA MAA ZAALEKA A’LAL LAAHE BE-A’ZEEZ.\nAnd nor this is hard for God.\nوَ لَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِّزْرَ اُخْرَىٰ ؕ وَاِنْ تَدْعُ مُثْقَلَةٌ اِلٰى حِمْلِهَا لَا يُحْمَلْ مِنْهُ شَىْءٌ وَّلَوْ كَانَ ذَا قُرْبٰى ؕ اِنَّمَا تُنْذِرُ الَّذِيْنَ يَخْشَوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ بِالْغَيْبِ وَاَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ ؕ وَمَنْ تَزَكّٰى فَاِنَّمَا يَتَزَكّٰى لِنَفْسِهٖ ؕ وَاِلَى اللّٰهِ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(18)\nWA LAA TAZERU WAAZERATUN WWEZRA AUKHRAA WA TAD-O’ MUSQALATUN ELAA HEMLEHAA LAA YUHMAL MINHO SHAY-UN WA LAW KAANA ZAL QURBAA INNAMAA TUNZERO LAZEENA YAKHSHAWNA RABBAHUM BIL-GHAYBE WA AQAAMUS SALAATA WA MAN TAZAKKAA FA-INNAMAA UATAZAKKAA LENAFSEHI WA ELAL LAAHE MASEER.\nAnd no bearer shall bear the burden of another; and if the heavy laden one should cry for (another bearer to carry) its burden, (even) aught of it shall not be carried, and even if he be near of kin; Thou canst but warn those who fear their Lord unseen and keep up regular prayer; And whosoever purifieth (himself), he only purifieth for his own self; And unto God (alone) is the destination (of all).\nوَمَا يَسْتَوِى الْاَعْمٰى وَالْبَصِيْرُ ۙ‏(19)\nWA MAA YASTAWEAA A-A’MAA WAL BASEERU.\nAnd alike are not (both) the blind and the seeing,\nوَلَا الظُّلُمٰتُ وَلَا النُّوْرُۙ‏(20)\nWA LAA AZ-ZULUMAATU WA LAA AN-NOORU.\nNor the darkness and the light\nوَلَا الظِّلُّ وَلَا الْحَرُوْرُۚ‏(21)\nWA LAA AZ-ZELLU WA LAA AL-HAROORU.\nNor the shade and the heat,\nوَمَا يَسْتَوِى الْاَحْيَآءُ وَلَا الْاَمْوَاتُ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُسْمِعُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ۚ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ بِمُسْمِعٍ مَّنْ فِى الْقُبُوْرِ‏(22)\nWA MAA YASTAWEAA AL-AAHYAAU WA LAA AL-AAMWAATU INNAL LAAHA YUSMEU’U MAN YASHAAA-O WA MAA ANTA BEMUSMEA’IN MAN FIL QOBOORE.\nAnd neither are alike (both) the living and the dead; Verily God heareth whom He willeth, and thou canst not make those hear who are in the graves.\nاِنْ اَنْتَ اِلَّا نَذِيْرٌ‏(23)\nIN ANTA ILLAA NAZEERUM.\nNone else art thou but a Warner.\nاِنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ بِالْحَقِّ بَشِيْرًا وَّنَذِيْرًاؕ وَاِنْ مِّنْ اُمَّةٍ اِلَّا خَلَا فِيْهَا نَذِيْرٌ‏(24)\nINNAA ARSALNAAKA BIL-HAQQE BASHEERANW WWANAZEERAN WA MIN UMMATIN ILLAA EZAA FEEHAA NAZEERUM.\nVerily We sent thee with truth, as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner: and there is not a people but a warner hath gone among them.\nوَاِنْ يُّكَذِّبُوْكَ فَقَدْ كَذَّبَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ‌ۚ جَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ وَبِالزُّبُرِ وَبِالْكِتٰبِ الْمُنِيْرِ‏(25)\nWA YYUKAZZEBOOKA FAQAD KAZZABA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM JAAA-AHUM JAAA-ATHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE WABEALZZUBURE WABEALKETAABE AL-MUNEERE.\nAnd if they belie thee, so indeed did belie those before them; their apostles had come unto them with clear proofs, and with scriptures, and with the enlightening Book.\nثُمَّ اَخَذْتُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا فَكَيْفَ كَانَ نَكِيْرِ‏(26)\nSUMMA AAKHAZTU LAZEENA KAFAROO FA-KAYFA KAANA NAKEER.\nThen did I seize those who disbelieved, so how (Severe) was the abhorrence (of Mine)?\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً‌ۚ فَاَخْرَجْنَا بِهٖ ثَمَرٰتٍ مُّخْتَلِفًا اَلْوَانُهَاؕ وَمِنَ الْجِبَالِ جُدَدٌۢ بِيْضٌ وَّحُمْرٌ مُّخْتَلِفٌ اَلْوَانُهَا وَغَرَابِيْبُ سُوْدٌ‏(27)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA ANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA AKH-RAJNAA BEHI SAMARAATIM MMUKHTALEFAN AALWAANUHAA WA MENAN JEBAALE JUDADUN BEEZUN WWAHUMRUN MMUKHTALEFUN AALWAANUHAA WAGHARAABEEBU SOODUN.\nSeest thou not that God sendeth down water from the heaven; then We bring forth with it fruits of various colours; and in the mountains are streaks white and red, of various colours, and (others) intensely black?\nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ وَالدَّوَآبِّ وَالْاَنْعَامِ مُخْتَلِفٌ اَ لْوَانُهٗ كَذٰلِكَ ؕ اِنَّمَا يَخْشَى اللّٰهَ مِنْ عِبَادِهِ الْعُلَمٰٓؤُا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَزِيْزٌ غَفُوْرٌ‏(28)\nWA MENAN NAASE WAALDDAWAABBE WAL AANA’AAME MUKHTALEFUN A’ZAABAN LWAANUH KAZAALEKA INNAMAA YAKHSHAA LAAHA MIN E’BAADEHIL AL-U’ULAMAAAUA INNAL LAAHA A’ZEEZUN GHAFOORUR.\nAnd of the people and beasts and cattle are of various colours likewise; verily fear God only those of His servants endued with knowledge: Verily, God is All-Mighty, Oft-Forgiving.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَتْلُوْنَ كِتٰبَ اللّٰهِ وَاَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاَنْفَقُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقْنٰهُمْ سِرًّا وَّعَلَانِيَةً يَّرْجُوْنَ تِجَارَةً لَّنْ تَبُوْرَۙ‏(29)\nINNAL LAZEENA YATLOONAL KETAABAL LAAHE WA AQAAMUS SALAATA WA ANFAQOO MIMMAA RAZAQNAAHUM SIRRAN WA A’LAANEYATAN YYARJOONA TEJAARATAN LAN-Y TABOORA.\nVerily, those who recite the Book of God and establish prayer and spend out of what We have provided them with, secretly and openly, hope for a merchandise which will never perish,\nلِيُوَفِّيَهُمْ اُجُوْرَهُمْ وَيَزِيْدَهُمْ مِّنْ فَضْلِهٖ ؕ اِنَّهٗ غَفُوْرٌ شَكُوْرٌ‏(30)\nLEEWAFFEEHUM AUJOORAHUM WAYAZEEDAHUM MIN FAZLEHI INNAHU GHAFOORUR SHAKOORUN.\nThat He may give them back their recompense (in full) and increase of His grace unto them; verily, He is Oft-Forgiving, the Greatest Appreciator (of Good)\nوَالَّذِىْۤ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ مِنَ الْكِتٰبِ هُوَ الْحَقُّ مُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِعِبَادِهٖ لَخَبِيْرٌۢ بَصِيْرٌ‏(31)\nWAL LAZEE AAWHAYNAA ELAYKA MENAL KETAABE HOWA HAQQO MOSADDEQAL LEMAA BAYNA YADAYHE INNAL LAAHA BE-E’BAADEHI LAKHABEERUN BASEER.\nAnd that which We have revealed unto thee of the Book, it is the truth testifying that which hath come before it; verily God, about His servants is All-Aware, All- Seeing.\nثُمَّ اَوْرَثْنَا الْكِتٰبَ الَّذِيْنَ اصْطَفَيْنَا مِنْ عِبَادِنَاۚ فَمِنْهُمْ ظَالِمٌ لِّنَفْسِهٖ‌ۚ وَمِنْهُمْ مُّقْتَصِدٌ‌ۚ وَمِنْهُمْ سَابِقٌۢ بِالْخَيْرٰتِ بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِؕ ذٰلِكَ هُوَ الْفَضْلُ الْكَبِيْرُؕ‏(32)\nSUMMA AAWRASNAA KETAABA LAZEENA ASTAFAYNAA MIN E’EBAADENAA FA-MINHUM ZAALEMUN LLENAFSEH WA MINHUM MMUQTASEDUN WA MINHUM SAABEQUN BIL-KHAYRAATE BE-IZNIL LAAH ZAALEKA HOWA FAZLUL KABEER.\nThen made We the inheritors of the Book (Qur’an) those whom chose We from among Our servants: and of them is he who causeth himself to suffer a loss, and of them is he who followeth the middle course, and of them is he who is the foremost in goodness by God’s permission: This is that which is the greatest excellence.\nجَنّٰتُ عَدْنٍ يَّدْخُلُوْنَهَا يُحَلَّوْنَ فِيْهَا مِنْ اَسَاوِرَ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ وَّلُؤْلُؤًا ۚ وَلِبَاسُهُمْ فِيْهَا حَرِيْرٌ‏(33)\nJANNAATU A’ADNIN YYADKHULOONAHAA YUHALLAWNA FEEHAA MIN ASAAWERA MIN ZAHABIN WWALULUAN WALEBAASUHUM FEEHAA HAREERUN.\nGardens of eternity they shall enter into, they shall be given to wear therein bracelets of gold and pearls, and their raiment therein be silk.\nوَقَالُوا الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْۤ اَذْهَبَ عَنَّا الْحَزَنَ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّنَا لَغَفُوْرٌ شَكُوْرُ ۙ‏(34)\nWA HAMDO LILLAAHE LAZEE AAZHABA WAGH AL-HAZANA INNAL RABBANAA LAGHAFOORUN SHAKOORU.\nAnd they shall say: “All praise is God’s (alone) Who hath taken away from us (all) grief; Verily our Lord is Oft-Forgiving, the Greatest Appreciator (of goodness)\nاۨلَّذِىْۤ اَحَلَّنَا دَارَ الْمُقَامَةِ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ‌ۚ لَا يَمَسُّنَا فِيْهَا نَصَبٌ وَّلَا يَمَسُّنَا فِيْهَا لُغُوْبٌ‏(35)\nLAZEE AAHALLANAA DAARA AL-MUQAAMATE MIN FAZLEHI LAA YAMASSUNAA FEEHAA NASABUN WA LAA YAMASSUNAA FEEHAA LUGHOOBUN.\nHe Who hath alighted us of His grace in an abode to abide (for ever); therein toucheth us not any toil, nor affecteth us therein any fatigue.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَهُمْ نَارُ جَهَنَّمَ‌ۚ لَا يُقْضٰى عَلَيْهِمْ فَيَمُوْتُوْا وَلَا يُخَفَّفُ عَنْهُمْ مِّنْ عَذَابِهَا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِىْ كُلَّ كَفُوْرٍۚ‏(36)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LAHUM NAARUL JAHANNAMA LAA YUQZAA A’LAYHIM FAYAMOOTOOA WA LAA YOKHAFFAFO A’NHUM MIN A’AZAABEHAA KAZAALEKA NAJZEAA KULLA KAFOORIN.\nAnd those who disbelieve, for them shall be the fire of Hell, it shall not be decreed that they should die, nor shall be lightened unto them aught of its torment; Thus do We retribute every ungrateful one.\nوَهُمْ يَصْطَرِخُوْنَ فِيْهَا ‌ۚ رَبَّنَاۤ اَخْرِجْنَا نَعْمَلْ صَالِحًا غَيْرَ الَّذِىْ كُنَّا نَعْمَلُؕ اَوَلَمْ نُعَمِّرْكُمْ مَّا يَتَذَكَّرُ فِيْهِ مَنْ تَذَكَّرَ وَجَآءَكُمُ النَّذِيْرُؕ فَذُوْقُوْا فَمَا لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ مِنْ نَّصِيْرٍ‏(37)\nWA HUM YASTAREKHOONA FEEHAA RABBANAA AAKHREJNAA NAA’MAL SAALEHAN GHAYRA LAZEE KUNNAA NAA’MALU AWALAM NUA’AMMERKUM MAA YATAZAKKARU FEEHE MAN TAZAKKARA WAJAAAKUMU AN-NAZEERU FA-ZOOQOO FAMAA LIZ-ZAALEMEENA MIN NNASEERIN.\nAnd they shall cry aloud therein for help: “O’ our Lord! Take us out (hence), we will do good deeds other than what we used to do (before).” (It shall be said unto them by the Lord): “Did not We keep you alive long enough for him who reflected to reflect therein? and came unto you the Warner (too); So (now) taste ye (the fruits of your deeds), then for the unjust there (shall be) no helper.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ عٰلِمُ غَيْبِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ اِنَّهٗ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(38)\nINNAL LAAHA A’ALEMUL GHAYBE SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ INNAHU A’LEEM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nVerily, God (alone) is the Knower of the unseen of the heavens and the earth; Verily He knoweth all that is in the breasts (hearts).\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَكُمْ خَلٰٓئِفَ فِى الْاَرْضِ ؕ فَمَنْ كَفَرَ فَعَلَيْهِ كُفْرُهٗ ؕ وَلَا يَزِيْدُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ كُفْرُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ اِلَّا مَقْتًا ۚ وَلَا يَزِيْدُ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ كُفْرُهُمْ اِلَّا خَسَارًا‏(39)\nHOWA LAZEE JAA’ALAKUM KHALAAAEFA FIL ARZE FAMAN KAFARA FA-A’LAYHE KUFROH WA LAA YAZEEDU KAAFEREEN KUFRUHUM I’NDAL RABBEHIM ILLAA MAQTAN WA LAA YAZEEDU KAAFEREEN KUFRUHUM ILLAA KHASAARAN.\nHe is the One Who made you the successors (of those who preceded you) in the earth; so whosoever disbelieveth against him shall be his disbelief; And the disbelief of the infidels shall increase not with their Lord but (His) wrath, and increaseth not the disbelief of the infidels but loss.\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ شُرَكَآءَكُمُ الَّذِيْنَ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ ؕ اَرُوْنِىْ مَاذَا خَلَقُوْا مِنَ الْاَرْضِ اَمْ لَهُمْ شِرْكٌ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ‌ ۚ اَمْ اٰتَيْنٰهُمْ كِتٰبًا فَهُمْ عَلٰى بَيِّنَتٍ مِّنْهُ ۚ بَلْ اِنْ يَّعِدُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ بَعْضُهُمْ بَعْضًا اِلَّا غُرُوْرًا‏(40)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM SHURAKAAAKUMU LAZEENA TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE AAROONEAA MAA KHALAQOOA MENAL ARZE AM LAHUM SHERKUN FIL SAMAAWAATE AM AATAYNAAHUM KETAABAA FAHUM A’LAA BAYNATIN MINHO BAL IN YYAE’EDU ZAALEMOON KHALAA BA’ZAN ILLAA GHOROORAA.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “See ye not your partners whom ye call upon other than God? Show me what part of the earth they have created, or have they any share in the heavens; or gave We unto them any scripture so that from it they (may give) proof (of their claim) Nay! Promise not the unjust unto one another of them but only to delude.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُمْسِكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ اَنْ تَزُوْلَا ۚوَلَئِنْ زَالَتَاۤ اِنْ اَمْسَكَهُمَا مِنْ اَحَدٍ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ حَلِيْمًا غَفُوْرًا‏(41)\nINNAL LAAHA YUMSEKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA AN TAZOOLAA, WA LA-IN ZAALATAA IN AMSAKAHOMAA MIN AHADIM MIM BA’DEH, INNAHU KAANA HALEEMAN GHAFOORAA.\nVerily, God holdeth the heavens and the earth lest they come to naught; and if they come to naught none besides Hirn can hold them back; Verily, He is the Most Forbearing, the Oft-Forgiving.\nوَاَ قْسَمُوْا بِاللّٰهِ جَهْدَ اَيْمَانِهِمْ لَئِنْ جَآءَهُمْ نَذِيْرٌ لَّيَكُوْنُنَّ اَهْدٰى مِنْ اِحْدَى الْاُمَمِۚ فَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ نَذِيْرٌ مَّا زَادَهُمْ اِلَّا نُفُوْرًا ۙ‏(42)\nWA QSAMOOA BIL-LAAHE JAHDA AAYMAANEHEM LAIL JAAA-AHUM NAZEERUM LLAYAKOONUNNA AHDAA MIN EHDAB AL-AUMAME FALAMMAA JAAA-AHUM NAZEERUM MAA ZAADAHUM ILLAA NUFOORAN.\nAnd swore they by God with the strongest oaths that if came unto them a warner, they would certainly be guided aright better than any other people; but when came unto them a warner it increased not in them but their aversion,\nاۨسْتِكْبَارًا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَكْرَ السَّيّیٴِؕ وَلَا يَحِيْقُ الْمَكْرُ السَّيِّئُ اِلَّا بِاَهْلِهٖ ؕ فَهَلْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَّا سُنَّتَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ ۚ فَلَنْ تَجِدَ لِسُنَّتِ اللّٰهِ تَبْدِيْلًا ۚ وَلَنْ تَجِدَ لِسُنَّتِ اللّٰهِ تَحْوِيْلًا‏(43)\nASTEKBAARAN FIL ARZE WAMAKRA AS-SAY WA LAA YAHEEQU AL-MAKRU AS-SAYU ILLAA BE-AHLEHI FA HAL YANZOROONA ILLAA SUNNATA AWWALEEN FALAN TAJEDA LESUNNATE LAAHE TABDEELAA WA LAN TAJEDA LESUNNATE LAAHE TAHWEELAN.\n(In) priding in the earth, and planning evil; and the evil plans {of theirs) shall beset not but the devisers themselves; Then wait they for aught save the course of the people gone before? For never shall thou find any change in the course of God; and never shalt thou find in the course of God any alteration.\nاَوَلَمْ يَسِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَيَنْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ وَكَانُوْۤا اَشَدَّ مِنْهُمْ قُوَّةً ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيُعْجِزَهٗ مِنْ شَىْءٍ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَلَا فِى الْاَرْضِ ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ عَلِيْمًا قَدِيْرًا‏(44)\nAWALAM YASEEROO FIL ARZE FAYANZOROO KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM WA KAANOO ASHADDA MINHUM QUWWAH WA MAA KAANA LAAHO LEEA’JEZAH MIN SHAY-IN FIL SAMAAWAATE WA LAA FIL ARZE INNAHU KAANA A’LEEMAN QADEERAA.\nHave they travelled not in the earth and seen how was the end of those before them though they were stronger than them in strength? And God is not such to frustrate Him aught in the heavens or in the earth; Verity He is the All-Knowing, All-Powerful\nوَلَوْ يُؤَاخِذُ اللّٰهُ النَّاسَ بِمَا كَسَبُوْا مَا تَرَكَ عَلٰى ظَهْرِهَا مِنْ دَآ بَّةٍ وَّلٰكِنْ يُّؤَخِّرُهُمْ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّىۚ فَاِذَا جَآءَ اَجَلُهُمْ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ كَانَ بِعِبَادِهٖ بَصِيْرًا‏(45)\nWA LAW YUAAKHEZU LAAHO NAASA BEMAA KASABOO MAA TARAKA A’LAA ZAHREHAA MIN DAABBATINW WA LAAKIL YYUAKKHERUHUM ELAA ELAA AJALIM FA-EZAA JAAA-A AAJALUHUM FA-INNAL LAAHA KAANA BE-E’BAADEHI BASEERAA.\nAnd were God to seize the people (to punish them) for what they wrought, He would leave not on the back of it (the earth) any moving being, but He respiteth them till an appointed term; and when cometh their doom, then verily God, about His servants is All-Seeing.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Faatir (The Originator)\nThere are 45 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. In a narration from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) it is said that three doors of Jannah will be opened for the person who recites this Surah. He will be able to enter it through whichever door he pleases. In another narration it is said that the eight doors of Jannah will open to him and he will be permitted to enter through whichever he likes.\nIt is narrated that a person once came to Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) and complained that his daughter had a problem of getting severe migraine headaches all the time. The Imam (a.s.) placed his hand on her head and recited verse 42 of this Surah and she was cured."
}
